/-
# LinnikContract — Tables.lean

The numerical tables of the contract (`rows15`, `rows14`, `table13`, frozen as `ℝ` data in
`Areas.lean`) are here given as **explicit rational data** (`rows15q`, `rows14q`, `table13q`,
of type `List ℚ`), together with the (proved) coercion lemmas identifying the two presentations.

This is the sense in which *every numerical input of the contract is an explicit rational
parameter* (deliverable item 5): the `ℝ` tables consumed by `Area3`/`Area4`/`Area7` are the
images of literal `ℚ` data, so every numerical verification about them is a rational
computation (`decide` / `norm_num`), and the transcendental quantities occurring in the
numerics of §4 are separate, explicitly listed parameters (see `Numerics.lean`).
-/
